# FinAssist Chatbot: Comprehensive Testing Guide

To thoroughly test your chatbot and ensure all capabilities—from basic data retrieval to advanced analytical features—are functioning correctly, try asking the following queries. They are grouped by feature and complexity.

## 1. Basic Account & Portfolio (User Data Test)
These queries test whether the chatbot correctly fetches and parses the `userData` (Orders, SIPs, Folios, etc.):
- *"What is my name and email registered with you?"*
- *"Show me my most recent orders."*
- *"How many active SIPs do I have right now?"*
- *"What is the total amount I have invested so far?"*
- *"List all my mutual fund folios."*

## 2. General Knowledge & RAG (FAQ Test)
These queries test the bot's ability to search the internal FAQs before resorting to general pre-trained knowledge:
- *"What is a Mutual Fund?"*
- *"How does compounding work?"*
- *"What is the difference between an SIP and a Lumpsum investment?"*
- *"Is it safe to invest in the stock market?"*

## 3. Explainable AI & Math (Chain-of-Thought Test)
These queries trigger the new **Glassmorphic `<thought>` accordion**. They force the AI to perform step-by-step calculations.
- *"If I start an SIP of ₹10,000 per month for the next 15 years, assuming an annual return of 12%, what will my final corpus be?"*
- *"Calculate the absolute return on my portfolio if I invested ₹50,000 and it is now worth ₹65,000."*
- *"If I have a lumpsum of ₹1,00,000, how many years will it take to double at a 15% CAGR?"*
- *"I want to save ₹20 Lakhs in 5 years. How much should my monthly SIP be assuming 10% returns?"*

## 4. Tax-Loss Harvesting (Optimization Test)
These queries test the newly injected backend utility that scans for underwater investments and calculates potential STCG/LTCG tax savings.
- *"Do I have any tax-loss harvesting opportunities in my portfolio?"*
- *"Can you check if I have any underwater investments that I can sell to offset capital gains?"*
- *"How can I optimize my current investments regarding taxes?"*
- *"I want to reduce my tax liability. Is my portfolio eligible for tax-loss harvesting?"*

## 5. Live Web Search & Sentiment Analytics (News Test)
These queries trigger the `search_web` python MCP tool and force the LLM to output a **Sentiment Score (0-100)**.
- *"Fetch the latest news for Reliance Industries. What is the current market sentiment?"*
- *"Give me a sentiment score for Apple stock based on today's headlines."*
- *"Is there any bad news about HDFC bank recently? Please provide the sentiment score."*
- *"Summarize the latest market news for SBI and tell me if the sentiment is bullish or bearish."*

## 6. Financial Tools & Live Data Retrieval (MCP Test)
These queries test the Python Server tools (Stock tools, mutual fund tools).
- *"Compare the performance of Parag Parikh Flexi Cap and Motilal Oswal midcap."*
- *"What are the top 5 stock holdings inside the SBI Small Cap fund?"*
- *"Show me the historical price chart for Tata Motors."* (if charting tool is implemented).
- *"What is the current estimated NAV of the Nippon India Growth Fund?"*

---
### 💡 Testing Pro-Tip
While testing, pay close attention to the **Chat UI**. Make sure that:
1. The AI responses are direct and professional.
2. The **"AI Reasoning Process"** accordion drops down smoothly with a glassmorphic background when mathematical questions are asked.
3. The responses use the Indian Rupee symbol (₹) and proper formatting.
